# Build trees (cloned + built inside .devcontainer/Dockerfile)
liboqs/
oqs-provider/

# Generated payloads and key material. Both are reproducible with
# `make payloads && make run`, and neither belongs in a repository linked from a
# paper: data/ is ~80 MB of random bytes, and out/ holds private keys
# (throwaway, but still private keys).
data/
out/

# results/ is deliberately NOT ignored. The figures and JSON in it are the
# numbers the manuscript cites, so they are committed as the record of the run
# that produced them -- every file there carries the same environment block and
# timestamp. Regenerate the whole directory with `make clean && make run`;
# never hand-edit or refresh one file out of it, because the value of the
# directory is that its files agree with each other.

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# Editor / OS
.vscode/
.DS_Store
